# Origin: Drive 007acc2 cross-family round R5 (2026-11-04_WISSEN_HexaNTK_R5_PRNR_CodeFactory_GPT6.md),
#   NTK-R5-NR03 "parameter check after the optimizer step is no rollback" / NTK-R5-PR04 "grad.isfinite before step";
#   never carried into this repo. Measured on main before writing any fix.

## Finding on main cd5f6dc (reproduction, single process, CPU)
# model: Linear(4,2) whose backward multiplies the gradient by NaN; loss finite; RunnerConfig(num_epochs=1, use_ema=True)
# runner.run() returned normally; the log said "Anomaly at step 1: NaN_or_Inf_Loss" (step 0 was the cause)
# params finite after run: False
# non-finite tensors in saved files:
#   last.pt            model_state_dict/lin.weight, lin.bias
#   resume_last.pt     model_state_dict/lin.weight, lin.bias, ema_state_dict/module.lin.weight, module.lin.bias
#   replay capsule     model_state_dict (already NaN at step 1)
# Cause: clip_grad_norm_ returns a NaN total norm and scales every gradient by it; optimizer.step() writes NaN;
#   EMA averages it in; the loss check before backward only sees the (finite) loss value.

